 # Sessions
 
+For maintainers changing login behavior or investigating a member's logout. Sessions keep members logged in across
+requests; the inactivity limit is now shorter so members are logged out sooner.
+
 ## Lifetime
 
-Each request renews the session for 30 minutes, `EXPIRY_MINUTES` in `larder/sessions.py`. Until March 2024 the limit
-was 10 minutes: members packing a pantry order on a slow mobile connection were logged out before they confirmed it
-and lost what they had picked, and support logged 120 tickets about it that month. The limit was raised to 30
-minutes, the shortest that ended those tickets.
+Each request renews the session for 10 minutes, set by
+[`EXPIRY_MINUTES`](../../larder/sessions.py). After 10 minutes without a request, the session expires.
+
+In March 2024, the limit was raised from 10 to 30 minutes after members packing a pantry order on a slow mobile
+connection were logged out before they confirmed it and lost what they had picked. Support logged 120 tickets
+about it that month; 30 minutes was the shortest limit that ended those tickets. The limit is now back to 10
+minutes to log members out sooner; those interruptions may recur.
 
